#describe what An update check that fails only because the machine is asleep or offline no longer logs a warning.
#describe before Update check failed: GitHub did not answer: net::ERR_NETWORK_IO_SUSPENDED appeared in Diagnostics.
#describe after Nothing is logged for sleep or offline errors; HTTP errors and malformed feeds still warn.
#describe verified pnpm test and pnpm run typecheck pass.
~ src/main/updater/feed.ts
~ src/main/updater/service.ts
~ test/updater-service.test.ts
#order src/main/updater/feed.ts
#order src/main/updater/service.ts
#order test/updater-service.test.ts
#reason src/main/updater/feed.ts A machine that is asleep or offline needs a way to be told apart from a real failure, so the warning can be skipped.
#reason src/main/updater/service.ts All three failure sites share one helper so an offline reason never reaches Diagnostics.
#reason test/updater-service.test.ts Pins that a suspended-network failure logs nothing while the check still reports failed.
#story Update check while the computer sleeps
#step actor Lantern
#step action checks for an update
